# `S-3d` infrastructure (decision 18): the api reached over IPv6 loopback — `env ipv6Loopback`'s base
# URL is `http://[::1]:4001/v1`. What is graded is that a bracketed IPv6 literal is a working base:
# the request goes out, a redirect's relative `Location` resolves against it, and a cookie set there
# is replayed there.

@edge @api
test "a bracketed IPv6 base URL reaches the api"
  api GET /edge/nulls
  expect status equals 200
  expect body.zero equals 0

@edge @api
test "a redirect under an IPv6 base resolves its Location against that base"
  api POST /edge/redirect/308 body {}
  expect status equals 200
  expect body.method equals "POST"

@edge @api
test "a cookie set under an IPv6 base is replayed to it"
  api GET /edge/cookies
  api GET /edge/cookies/echo
  expect body.cookie contains "edge_plain=1"
